## 3A. Source-conflict ledger — must be settled before an event is issued

| Conflict / gap | Current reconciliation | Release treatment |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Match outcome, bracket advancement, and individual Damage prizes | Recurring bracket advancement follows the verified match outcome calculated from published individual-performance metrics under the approved scoring method and D21 tie-breaks. Participant-level Damage/`dblns` outputs remain traceable inputs/outputs; any additional award or seeding use must be explicitly published. Pilot placement is by total individual Damage for its announced awards; if a Pilot bracket is used, its outcome calculation must be published separately before signup. | Policy aligned; event-specific formula, awards, and tie-break wording still require approval. |
| Pilot vs recurring entry and lineup visibility | Pilot is drop-in and uses visible lineups; recurring format uses weekly individual registration, roster lock, and hidden lineups until ready-up/setup checks. | Resolved by format; do not transfer settings across formats. |
| Pilot special armor-mode label | The source names conflict (“Armor Resilience” vs “Armor Resilient Test”). **Default for this release: omit the special-mode match and use only verified 10-minute Standard Battle modes** until an authorized host verifies the exact current-client mode label. Do not announce a special-mode game under an unverified name. | BLOCKING — verify the mode label in the installed client or formally omit the special-mode match from the event schedule. |
| Recurring Race-event placement | **Selected template rule:** Race is a separate side-event, scheduled one hour before the normal event on weeks 3, 6, 9, and the finale (week 12 if a 12-week season is adopted). The regular map rotation is independent; “Big Race” at weeks 3 and 10 is treated as a map name, not the side-event. Race damage contributes to cumulative season/Race standings and any declared Race award, not the regular match score for that night. Actual dates and the organizer-approved schedule remain required. | BLOCKING — organizer must ratify this template policy and publish actual dates/time zone; do not treat the 12-week template as a booked schedule. |
| Recurring team/bot composition | **Selected safe default:** every regular recurring stage must publish exact human/bot slots and use equal total team sizes of either 6 or 9 slots; human participants may not be silently converted to a different team size. The source’s “2v6 against bots” Round 1 wording does not unambiguously specify both sides; **do not schedule Round 1 until the organizer signs a per-side roster table**. Later stage rosters use 2–3 humans per side with bots filling to the declared 6- or 9-slot size. | BLOCKING — sign the exact Round 1 roster and publish all stage human/bot slots. |
| Ship limits and lists | Source gives tier limits and prohibits human carriers/submarines, but the allowed/banned ship tables are blank. **Default rule:** use an explicit published allowlist; an unlisted ship is not approved. The event cannot open registration until the current allowlist and any event bans are attached. | BLOCKING — publish a current allowable/banned list and exact tier/ship rules before signup. |
| Missing event values | Dates/times, actual schedule, exact map rotation, exact prize values, owner/approver, contacts, and effective time are not in the source files. | BLOCKING — do not treat this reusable template as a scheduled event notice. |

## 4. Selected working scoring-policy decisions C01–C06

<div style="background-color:#DFF2FF; border:1.5px solid #0070C0; padding:6px 8px; margin:4px 0;"><strong>⚓ Quick hint:</strong> Do not announce or issue the event until required settings, ownership, approvals, and release gates are complete.</div>
| ID | Selected working policy | Implementation / approval consequence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| C01 — Round 3 Race/time | Input is positive elapsed seconds; per-game metric target is 1 / elapsed_seconds, so lower time scores better. Blank, nonnumeric, zero, negative, or non-finite values block score certification until corrected. | Historical formula behaves contrary to this target. Canonical workbook/calculator implementation and regression are OPEN. |
| C02 — Class weights | Shared map is DD=4, CA=3, BB=2. Blank/unsupported classes are errors, not implicit zero. | Canonical implementation must derive the weight from class or validate label/weight as a pair; parity tests OPEN. |
| C03 — S10:S12 preferences | Retire/hide class-preference controls from participant-facing scoring. They do not affect the observed formula. | Do not change historic source; retire in future approved UI/workbook and confirm by test. |
| C04 — Round 4 pool control | Retire/hide F8 from participant-facing scoring. It does not affect the observed Round-4 formula. | Do not imply it changes Round-4 score or pool distribution. Any future use requires a new policy/formula and full regression. |
| C05 — Dollar display | OFF by default in participant-facing views. H12 is internal historical QA only; it is not a prize or currency value. | Any future public display requires a verified basis, separate organizer approval, and the exact illustrative-only disclaimer. |
| C06 — Changes after start | Freeze ordinary rules/settings after start; apply changes prospectively to future/unplayed games only, never retroactively to completed games. Narrow safety/security/platform emergencies require written reason, scope, authorizer, times, affected games, notice to both team representatives, and independent review where feasible. | Preserve raw-input correction history separately from policy changes; record every override. |

These are the selected governing working policies recorded in v3.15. Implementation tests and the authorized organizer signature remain separate blocking gates.

